      "CVE": "CVE-2026-42493",
      "Description": "Addressing certain issues, in particular related to operations which may\ntake excessively long and therefore would need preemption, has turned out\noverly costly.  Since alternatives (HVM/PVH: HAP, PV: shim) are commonly\navailable, the decision was to deprecate the functionality, while still\nretaining it for people to use at their own (security) risk.  Memory-wise\nsmall enough guests may still be okay to run.",
      "Threats": [
        {
          "Type": "Impact",
          "Severity": "moderate"
